WEBVTT

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:35.990
<b>Sakura and Meiling's Friend</b>

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:43.740
Over there!

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:48.990
What the heck is that?!

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:53.950
Something's underground!

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:56.250
It stopped!

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:03.400
It's gonna get out!

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:04.890
We have to stop it!

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:08.020
<b>Siege</b>

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:08.670
You think you can enclose 
this whole, huge garden?

00:02:09.050 --> 00:02:10.080
<i>Siege!</i>

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:19.330
Surround the entire mansion!

00:02:31.180 --> 00:02:34.080
What's happening?!

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:55.480
Ya did it...

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:00.690
All right... It's closed in.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:05.870
What's goin' on?

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:11.630
It turned back this way!

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.090
Oh, no! Tomoyo's house!

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:15.140
Kero-chan!

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:15.830
Right!

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:27.220
Is this house gonna be okay?!

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:29.690
Sakura-chan!

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.510
Aw, man! The maze is ruined!

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:44.030
Tomoyo-chan! Akiho-chan!

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:45.020
We have to hurry!

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:49.530
Sakura...

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.170
Shoot! I can't catch up!

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:03.710
There, it is...

00:04:03.710 --> 00:04:04.890
Go, Sakura!

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:08.290
<i>Force without master,</i>

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:13.490
<i>heed the call of my Staff of Dreams, 
and become my power!</i>

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:15.980
<i>Secure!</i>

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:37.490
"Swing"...

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.670
Sakura, way to go!

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:42.670
<b>Swing</b>

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:47.470
But the house and garden are...

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:49.390
Nah, you did great!

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:51.170
We'll apologize later.

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:55.430
Thanks for doing such a good job.

00:04:59.950 --> 00:05:02.500
W-Wait... Wait!

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:06.640
It sure likes her a lot...

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:09.750
Tomoyo-chan!

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:14.100
Sakura-chan! Are you all right?

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.940
Yeah, I'm okay.

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.110
I made it a card.

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:21.140
But some trees in your garden fell over...

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:26.130
As long as you and Kero-chan are 
okay, that's all that matters.

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:28.280
Tomoyo-chan...

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:29.520
Tomoyo...

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:34.760
Besides, I'm sure Kero-chan captured 
some splendid footage for me.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:39.440
I can't wait to see it later!

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:45.050
That quake really took me by surprise!

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:46.730
Are you all okay?

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:48.610
Y-Yes.

00:05:48.610 --> 00:05:49.990
We're all right.

00:05:51.570 --> 00:05:53.540
What's wrong, Akiho-chan?

00:05:54.610 --> 00:05:59.450
I fell asleep while visiting 
a friend's house again...

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:05.800
Ya couldn't help it. It was magic.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:09.490
I fell asleep, too, for some reason.

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:13.880
Couldn't help that, either. It was magic.

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:18.140
Regardless, I'm so glad 
everyone is all right!

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:19.360
Me, too.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:22.240
None of you were hurt, right?

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:23.140
Right!

00:06:23.610 --> 00:06:25.770
Would you like more tea?

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:27.390
Yes, please!

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:34.160
I wanna eat some, too!

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.920
Please take care getting home.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:43.080
Come visit again, anytime.

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:45.000
Oh, I almost forgot! Sakura-chan!

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:46.290
Yes?

00:06:49.100 --> 00:06:56.020
Grandfather was very curious as to how 
you planned to spend your summer.

00:06:57.400 --> 00:07:00.880
I'm sure he'd love to see 
you at the villa again!

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:04.410
I'll talk to my dad, 
and get in touch with him.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:10.200
Tomoyo-san's mother was a lovely person!

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:12.230
She's beautiful and a great cook.

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:16.370
I know! The clotted cream was so good!

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:19.950
Tomoyo-chan said she'd ask 
her mom for the recipe.

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:20.910
Really?

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:24.200
My afternoon tea...

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:27.920
Well, I'm heading this way.

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:30.550
Thank you for having me along today!

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.020
Thank you for coming.

00:07:32.020 --> 00:07:34.430
I'll send you the pictures I took, later.

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:35.170
Okay.

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:37.710
See you at school, Akiho-chan.

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:39.170
Okay, see you.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:57.320
You seem in high spirits.

00:07:57.730 --> 00:07:58.960
Kaito-san?

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:02.890
What brings you out here?

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:07.540
Your message said you were on your 
way home, so I came to meet you.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:10.580
Thank you.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:15.190
As always, you sing so beautifully.

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:18.030
Huh? Y-You could hear me?!

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.400
Quite clearly.

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:26.600
The friend whose home you visited 
today is also a good singer, yes?

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:30.500
Yes, we're both in the Chorus Club.

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:37.670
Oh, right... Her mother prepared 
a delicious afternoon tea for us.

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:41.290
I can see you had a nice time.

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:42.250
Yes!

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:51.530
My family has visited many countries

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:53.910
to collect the books we searched for.

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:57.940
But sometimes, we'd leave the country 
immediately after finding one,

00:08:57.940 --> 00:09:01.750
so I wasn't able to make many 
friends in those countries.

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:05.290
Of course, that might have 
been my own fault...

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:09.210
You are a wonderful person, Akiho-san.

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:15.790
But here, I made friends right away.

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:18.090
All very nice people.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:19.250
They really are.

00:09:19.730 --> 00:09:21.560
Which of them are you closest to?

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:23.330
Sakura-san.

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:26.550
Sakura Kinomoto-san, was it?

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:31.090
Yes. She's so kind, and she's very cute.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:35.700
She said she'd show me her family's 
library, next time I visit.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:37.710
That sounds very exciting.

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:41.960
I hear her father specializes in archaeology,

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:44.350
so he might have some very interesting books.

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:50.090
Have I mentioned Sakura-san's 
father to you before?

00:09:56.990 --> 00:09:58.140
Kaito-san?

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:20.650
<i>Tina Rie Triax.</i>

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:25.400
<i>Time, in accordance with 
the covenant, turn back.</i>

00:10:46.230 --> 00:10:47.100
Huh?

00:10:47.560 --> 00:10:49.100
What's the matter?

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:51.320
Huh? What?

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:56.970
You said Sakura-san is going to 
show you her family's library?

00:10:56.970 --> 00:11:00.210
Oh... Yes, that's right!

00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:02.410
That sounds very exciting.

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:05.480
What shall I make for you 
to take to her house?

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:09.700
U-Um, could I make something with you?

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:10.940
Of course.

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:14.310
Thank you!

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:36.200
That's what I call "birds of a 
feather flocking together."

00:11:36.200 --> 00:11:37.080
Huh?

00:11:37.080 --> 00:11:39.060
You and Shinomoto-san.

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:41.710
You're so alike, and not just 
because of your names!

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:45.040
Are we?

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:46.130
Hasn't anyone told you?

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:47.250
They have.

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:48.010
I thought so.

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:03.340
What are the people you know like?

00:12:03.340 --> 00:12:05.530
They're all really nice.

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:09.760
When you believe all the people 
around you are good,

00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:11.960
you attract only good people...

00:12:12.380 --> 00:12:15.540
And when you believe all the 
people around you are bad,

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:18.240
you don't notice when you meet good people.

00:12:19.210 --> 00:12:20.550
But you know...

00:12:21.250 --> 00:12:25.300
Sometimes, watching good 
people makes me feel sad.

00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:33.640
Who's that?

00:12:36.390 --> 00:12:37.680
Someone you know?

00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:38.650
No.

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:44.660
Kinomoto-san!

00:12:47.490 --> 00:12:48.800
What's with this girl?!

00:12:55.770 --> 00:12:56.630
Meiling-chan!

00:13:09.850 --> 00:13:11.610
Are you okay, Kinomoto-san?

00:13:11.610 --> 00:13:12.970
Th-Thanks...

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:16.910
So, what is that?

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:18.570
I'm pretty sure it's a card,

00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:20.180
but I didn't sense anything—

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:31.200
I see you're as athletic as ever!

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:35.680
That did it!

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:40.290
What's going on?!

00:13:41.240 --> 00:13:42.870
Hey! What do we do now?!

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:47.130
There was a Clow Card a bit like this, too!

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:49.820
But there were two of them then!

00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:51.630
Syaoran and I took them out together!

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:55.020
They were sort of like 
twins, acting together.

00:13:56.560 --> 00:13:57.410
Hey...

00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:00.930
Over here!

00:14:01.390 --> 00:14:02.890
No, over here!

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:05.160
Meiling-chan!

00:14:06.190 --> 00:14:07.400
It's all right!

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:10.660
What do I do now?!

00:14:11.650 --> 00:14:15.170
If it's like The Twin, maybe it'll 
turn into a card the same way!

00:14:15.170 --> 00:14:17.650
But there's only one, this time!

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:23.470
The shoulders!

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:25.930
If we break the stones on both 
shoulders, at the same time...

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:29.540
Kinomoto-san...

00:14:29.540 --> 00:14:30.140
Right!

00:14:31.160 --> 00:14:32.960
Move as I do.

00:14:32.960 --> 00:14:33.610
Right!

00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:34.630
Here it comes.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:37.850
Left!

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:38.550
Okay!

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:39.920
Now, right!

00:14:40.430 --> 00:14:41.260
Okay!

00:14:41.260 --> 00:14:42.260
Back, three times.

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:42.800
Okay!

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:43.620
Jump!

00:14:46.790 --> 00:14:47.670
Here goes.

00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:48.150
Yeah!

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:01.790
Now!

00:15:04.560 --> 00:15:06.850
<i>Key that hides the forces of dreams!</i>

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:11.940
<i>Show me your true form!</i>

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:14.920
<i>Release!</i>

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:36.990
<i>Force without master,</i>

00:15:37.320 --> 00:15:40.700
<i>heed the call of my Staff of Dreams, 
and become my power!</i>

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:42.130
<i>Secure!</i>

00:15:57.380 --> 00:15:59.570
She really did turn into a card...

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:01.560
"Struggle"...

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:04.520
Struggle.

00:16:06.090 --> 00:16:07.400
Meiling-chan, are you okay?!

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:09.140
Are you hurt?

00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:11.170
Your cheek is red!

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:14.080
It's just a scratch.

00:16:15.810 --> 00:16:18.910
What's up? Are we home already?

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:23.420
We've been through a lot today. 
Let's take grab a bath and go to bed.

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:34.930
I still managed to turn it into a 
card, with Meiling-chan's help.

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:37.000
Don't feel so bad.

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:40.680
I was asleep at the most important moment...

00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:47.840
What if Tomoyo finds out 
I didn't get it on video?!

00:16:48.380 --> 00:16:57.210
What do I do? This is bad. 
What do I do? This is bad.

00:16:51.670 --> 00:16:53.120
<i>That's</i> why you feel bad?

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:55.120
Come in!

00:16:58.210 --> 00:16:59.690
Thanks for the bath.

00:16:59.690 --> 00:17:01.520
Your cut didn't sting?

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:04.850
I'm fine. You're such a worrywart.

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:06.940
Let me dry your hair.

00:17:06.940 --> 00:17:08.970
Sure, but aren't you tired?

00:17:08.970 --> 00:17:11.460
Nope! I'm fine!

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:16.530
Should I apologize in advance,

00:17:16.530 --> 00:17:21.640
or should I bring it up tomorrow, 
in passing, like it's no big deal?

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:23.880
I'm sorry.

00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:25.650
For what?

00:17:26.470 --> 00:17:29.660
I put you in danger...

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.650
But you know, it made me happy!

00:17:36.670 --> 00:17:41.410
You and I haven't ever really done 
anything together before.

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:45.310
You helped me a lot when I 
was gathering Clow Cards,

00:17:45.310 --> 00:17:47.460
but it was never just the two of us.

00:17:47.930 --> 00:17:52.190
It made me really happy to do 
our best at something together.

00:17:52.190 --> 00:17:53.390
Thank you!

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:00.750
Well, good!

00:18:02.990 --> 00:18:07.720
I was wondering how I'd yell at you, 
if you'd kept apologizing to me.

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:14.370
It made me happy to capture a card 
with you for the first time, too.

00:18:14.760 --> 00:18:16.120
Meiling-chan...

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:18.550
Hey.

00:18:19.380 --> 00:18:24.610
Do you remember what I said when we 
were leaving Daidouji-san's house?

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:31.610
That watching good people makes 
you feel sad, sometimes...

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:33.120
Did it make you curious?

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:34.880
Yeah...

00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:39.930
There are lots of different 
types of "good people."

00:18:40.710 --> 00:18:46.160
But the people around me are always 
thinking of everyone else's happiness

00:18:46.160 --> 00:18:49.650
and how to make everyone else smile.

00:18:50.630 --> 00:18:53.100
That's a really good thing,

00:18:53.100 --> 00:18:56.460
but if all you think about is other people,

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:59.660
you stop caring about yourself.

00:19:00.350 --> 00:19:04.340
Aren't you and Syaoran doing too 
much for those you care about

00:19:04.340 --> 00:19:06.990
and forgetting to care about yourselves?

00:19:09.300 --> 00:19:13.140
That's especially true for Syaoran. 
Plus, he's stubborn.

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:18.300
You should find your own happiness, 
first, and make him open his eyes.

00:19:19.220 --> 00:19:20.680
Can I do that?

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:22.920
Don't think you can?

00:19:24.830 --> 00:19:29.390
I just feel like... a lot 
of things are different.

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:32.430
And I don't just mean the new cards.

00:19:32.950 --> 00:19:36.640
It feels like something really 
important is different.

00:19:38.930 --> 00:19:41.690
I don't know anything about the cards,

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:45.940
but you have the most powerful 
magic words of all, don't you?

00:19:49.670 --> 00:19:52.820
"I'm sure I'll be all right!"

00:19:52.820 --> 00:19:54.330
That's right!

00:19:55.600 --> 00:19:59.550
Hey, should I apologize right now 
or save my own skin for today?

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:01.330
What do you think?

00:20:04.330 --> 00:20:05.720
Thank you so much.

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:07.920
You're welcome.

00:20:08.260 --> 00:20:10.310
I appreciate all you've done for me.

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:15.340
Oh, not at all. I'm sorry I couldn't 
be at home very much.

00:20:15.640 --> 00:20:18.220
Kinomoto-san did her best to take care of me.

00:20:18.220 --> 00:20:21.870
I heard you taught her how to 
make some Chinese dishes.

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:24.850
I can't wait to have her make them for me.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:34.540
<b>Private</b>

00:20:27.920 --> 00:20:30.520
I'll leave her to you, then.

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:35.500
You don't want to see 
Syaoran-kun before you go?

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:38.920
Nah. If anything happens, 
he'll come to Hong Kong.

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:42.640
Besides, I accomplished almost 
everything I came here for.

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:43.920
Almost?

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:45.110
Hey!

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:46.420
Y-Yes?

00:20:47.510 --> 00:20:51.360
Can I call you "Sakura" from now on, too?

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:53.860
Of course!

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:57.510
And that makes 100% of what I came here for!

00:21:13.510 --> 00:21:15.460
See you again, Sakura!

00:21:17.050 --> 00:21:19.920
See you, Meiling-chan!

00:21:20.220 --> 00:21:22.030
Take care!

00:21:31.380 --> 00:21:32.220
<i>Hello?</i>

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:37.700
I told you I'd take you to the airport.

00:21:37.700 --> 00:21:39.820
<i>I can get there myself.</i>

00:21:39.820 --> 00:21:42.040
<i>Honestly, you're both such worrywarts!</i>

00:21:42.430 --> 00:21:43.440
Both?

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:46.400
Oh, by the way...

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:51.560
I'll be calling Kinomoto-san 
"Sakura" from now on, too.

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:53.890
<i>Huh? What brought that on?</i>

00:21:53.890 --> 00:21:56.210
Well, we've fought together now.

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:59.570
<i>You fought... Wait, did something happen?</i>

00:21:59.570 --> 00:22:03.020
Well, I'm not sure. Why don't 
you ask Sakura yourself?

00:22:03.430 --> 00:22:05.070
<i>Come on, Meiling...</i>

00:22:16.360 --> 00:22:21.670
<i>I don't know what it is you know 
or why you came to Japan.</i>

00:22:22.660 --> 00:22:27.720
<i>But if anything happens to you, 
I know who'll be the saddest.</i>

00:22:29.460 --> 00:22:31.810
<i>I'm Sakura's friend, too.</i>

00:22:32.610 --> 00:22:34.850
<i>If you make her cry, you'll regret it.</i>

00:22:36.780 --> 00:22:37.780
Yeah.

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:12.130
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:12.970
<b>Leave It to Kero-chan!</b>

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:16.010
Where the wind takes you, as your heart 
leads you... to "Leave It to Kero-chan!"

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:18.600
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:18.600
<b>K</b>

00:24:16.010 --> 00:24:18.590
Today, I'm introducin' Yuna D. Kaito!

00:24:18.590 --> 00:24:21.730
As Akiho's butler, he looks after her 
with both elegance and a smile.

00:24:21.730 --> 00:24:24.310
He's also a great cook. The cake 
he made was super tasty.

00:24:24.310 --> 00:24:26.690
